    ss.set_defaults(func=cmd_serve)

    sq = _sp(sub, "search", "find models that fit this machine", """
examples:
  llcpp search qwen3 coder                        keyword search
  llcpp search "fast coding model under 20gb"     size cap and intent parsed
  llcpp search "best vision model I can run"      filters to multimodal repos
  llcpp search --llm "good for autocomplete"      local model expands + reranks
  llcpp search mistral --vram 16                  pretend a smaller budget

Only models that fit are shown; --all includes the rest. Results carry an
estimated tok/s for this machine and flags for mtp, vision and moe.

Hugging Face matches repo NAMES, not descriptions, so a long sentence is
narrowed to keywords first. --llm instead asks a running local model for
several name guesses, then has it rerank what came back, which handles
requests that never name a model. See `llcpp help hardware`.
""")
    sq.add_argument("query", nargs="+", help="keywords or plain English")
    sq.add_argument("-n", "--limit", type=int, default=10, help="results to show")
